{
  "about": "What softn.time answers, as both SoftN backend hosts must answer it. Each case is one call, softn.time[call](...args), made by `script` in a handler: `result` is what it returns, `throws` says it throws, and `same` names other arguments for which the call returns the same thing (age depends on the day it is asked). The PHP host is the reference: the text of format() is what its Node gave when this was written, kept by both hosts in tables of their own so that neither drifts with a locale library. Read by apps/softn-host-php/tests/route-declarations.test.mjs and apps/softn-host-rust/src/bridges/time.rs.",
  "script": "function timeCases(req){var out=[];for(var i=0;i<req.body.cases.length;i++){var c=req.body.cases[i];try{out.push({ok:softn.time[c.call].apply(null,c.args)});}catch(e){out.push({threw:true});}}return {status:200,rollback:true,body:out};}",
